From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 06:41:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Dims-only image loads for out-of-isolate rendering (renderer
 mode)

DocumentConfig::dims_only_images routes every ImageHandler through a
header-only dimension sniff (image crate into_dimensions; no RGBA
decode) and stores the original encoded bytes in the node's replaced
slot via Resource::EncodedImage -> RasterImageData{encoded:true}.
Layout only ever reads width/height, so intrinsic sizing is exact
(better than the decode-cap path, which downscales dims too).

Local raster consumers that DO need pixels (canvas drawImage, the
legacy in-isolate screenshot/PDF path) call the new
kitesurf_materialize_node_image / kitesurf_materialize_encoded_images
to decode in place (capped, damage-marked). Undecodable bytes drop to
ImageData::None so vello never sees garbage.

Why: the embedder's renderer mode paints in a separate isolate.
Decoded RGBA is the dominant page heap cost (4000x3000 jpeg: ~2 MB
encoded vs ~48 MB decoded); shipping encoded bytes also beats the
recorder's lossless-WebP re-encode on both size and CPU.
